      "title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Adminsitration/Compliance",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Adminsitration/Compliance - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Graduate Assistant-Athletic Adminsitration/Compliance American International College in Springfield, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Application Due: Open Until Filled Category: Athletics - Athletic Administration Position Summary The Graduate Assistant for Athletic Administration/Compliance will work under the direct supervision of the Director of Athletics Compliance to support the day-to-day administration of the athletics department and ensure institutional adherence to NCAA, conference, and institutional rules and regulations. This position is intended for a graduate student pursuing an advanced degree who is seeking hands-on, applied experience in intercollegiate athletics administration while completing academic coursework. The Graduate Assistant will gain broad exposure to compliance monitoring, eligibility certification, recruiting regulation, and general athletics department operations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Assist with the interpretation, communication, and monitoring of NCAA, conference, and institutional rules and regulations across all sport programs. • Support the initial and continuing eligibility certification process for student-athletes, including tracking academic progress, satisfactory progress toward a degree, and amateurism status. • Assist with the monitoring and processing of financial aid, including athletic scholarship agreements, renewals, reductions, and cancellations. • Help track and audit recruiting activity, including official and unofficial visits, contact and evaluation periods, and phone/electronic correspondence logs. • Assist with the administration of playing and practice season limitations (countable athletically related activity/CARA logs). • Support the processing of transfer paperwork, including notification of transfer and transfer portal entries. • Help coordinate rules education sessions for coaches, staff, student-athletes, and boosters. • Assist with the preparation and organization of documentation for NCAA and conference reporting requirements, including squad lists and required annual reports. • Support day-to-day athletics administration tasks, which may include event management, facility scheduling, or department communications as assigned. • Maintain accurate, organized compliance records and assist with internal audits of departmental files. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics Compliance or department administration. Required Qualifications • Bachelor's degree completed prior to the start of the assistantship, and current acceptance into (or enrollment in) a graduate degree program at the institution. • Strong working knowledge of, or demonstrated interest in, NCAA rules and regulations. • Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. • Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage confidential information appropriately. • Proficiency with standard office software (e.g., Microsoft Office/Excel); ability to learn compliance software and database systems. • Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team-oriented department. • Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, based on athletic event and recruiting schedules. Preferred Qualifications • Coursework, internship, or prior work experience in athletic administration, compliance, or sport management. • Familiarity with NCAA compliance software (e.g., ARMS, JumpForward, Teamworks Compliance, or similar). • Familiarity with the NCAA Legislative Services Database (LSDBi) or eligibility center processes. Time Commitment & Terms This is a part-time graduate assistantship tied to concurrent enrollment in a graduate program. The position typically requires 20–29 hours per week, with schedule demands fluctuating based on the athletics event calendar, recruiting periods, and compliance reporting deadlines. Compensation includes a stipend and/or tuition assistance in accordance with department and graduate school policy; specific terms will be outlined at the time of offer. To Apply Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references to the Deputy Athletic Director for Compliance and Administration Scott Foulis ( scott.foulis@aic.edu ) and Director of Athletics Rob Kearney (Robert.kearney@aic.edu). Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. AIC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply Now Related Searches: Athletics - Athletic Administration Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: scott.foulis@aic.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Upd