    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179597912&Title=Head%20Equipment%20Manager": {
      "title": "Head Equipment Manager",
      "description": "Head Equipment Manager - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Head Equipment Manager American International College in Springfield, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $50,000 - $55,000 per year Posted: 5 days ago Category: Athletics - Athletic Administration About AIC Athletics American International College in Springfield, Massachusetts sponsors 22 varsity programs and approximately 650 student-athletes, competing primarily in the Northeast-10 Conference. The department is built on grit, resilience and a team-first mentality. We embrace our underdog identity and believe success comes from everyone working toward a common goal. Position Summary The Head Equipment Manager leads all athletic equipment and uniform operations for AIC Athletics. This person makes sure every team has safe, properly fitted and well-maintained equipment and uniforms for practice, competition and travel. The Head Equipment Manager runs the equipment room day to day, manages inventory and purchasing, and supervises the Assistant Equipment Manager and a staff of student work-study employees. The role works closely with coaches, athletic trainers, and facilities and operations staff, with particular focus on the demands of football and ice hockey. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Supervision and Staffing Serve as direct supervisor to the Assistant Equipment Manager, including setting their work schedule, assigning sport coverage, and conducting annual goal setting and performance reviews. Serve as direct supervisor to student work-study employees, including hiring, training, setting work schedules around academic commitments, approving timesheets and evaluating performance. Build equipment room coverage schedules that support practice, competition and travel needs across all sports. Equipment Operations Oversee the purchase, issue, fitting, collection, cleaning, repair and storage of athletic equipment and uniforms for all varsity and club programs. Lead football equipment operations, including helmet and shoulder pad fitting, game-day setup, sideline support and travel. Lead ice hockey equipment operations, including skate sharpening and repair, helmet and protective equipment fitting, bench support and travel (when necessary). Manage laundry operations for practice and game apparel. Prepare, pack and transport equipment for away competitions, and travel with teams as assigned. Safety and Compliance Manage the annual helmet reconditioning and recertification process to NOCSAE standards, and keep accurate records for all protective equipment. Make sure all equipment meets NCAA, conference and manufacturer safety standards and rules of play. Work with the sports medicine staff on protective equipment needs, custom fittings and injury-related modifications. Inventory, Budget and Vendors Maintain an accurate inventory system for all equipment, uniforms and apparel, including annual audits. Manage the equipment budget, and prepare purchase orders and annual ordering timelines with head coaches. Serve as primary contact with equipment and apparel vendors, and support the department's apparel partnership and branding standards. Keep the equipment room and storage areas clean, organized and secure. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Sport Administration or a comparable program 2+ years of experience in athletic equipment operations Hands-on experience with football and ice hockey equipment operations Supervisory experience with staff or student workers Strong organizational, inventory management and communication skills Valid driver's license and successful completion of a background check Preferred Qualifications Certification from the Athletic Equipment Managers Association (AEMA) Experience at the NCAA level Experience with skate sharpening and hockey equipment repair Experience with helmet fitting and NOCSAE reconditioning processes Experience with equipment inventory software and budget management Working Conditions and Physical Demands Irregular hours, including evenings, weekends and holidays, based on practice and competition schedules. Regular team travel, including overnight trips. Indoor, outdoor and ice rink work in varied conditions. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds, stand for long periods, and operate laundry and equipment repair machinery. AIC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply Now Related Searches: Athletics - Athletic Administration Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Updated) Privacy Policy"
