    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179597910&Title=Assist%20Athletic%20Dir%2C%20Sports%20Med%20%26%20Performance": {
      "title": "Assist Athletic Dir, Sports Med & Performance",
      "description": "Assist Athletic Dir, Sports Med & Performance - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Assist Athletic Dir, Sports Med & Performance American International College in Springfield, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $75,000 - $90,000 per year Posted: 5 days ago Category: Athletics - Athletic Administration About AIC Athletics American International College in Springfield, Massachusetts sponsors 22 NCAA Division II varsity programs and approximately 600 student-athletes, competing in the Northeast-10 Conference. The department is built on grit, resilience and a team-first mentality. We embrace our underdog identity and believe that success comes from everyone working toward a common goal - and that comprehensive care for the whole student-athlete is central to that success. Position Summary The Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine and Performance leads all athletic training and sports performance services for AIC Athletics. This person sets the standard of care for nearly 650 student-athletes, manages and develops the sports medicine and strength and conditioning staff, and serves as the department's primary connection to campus health services, the team physician group and our physical therapy partners. As a member of the department's senior leadership team, the Assistant AD helps shape departmental policy, budget and strategy. The position also carries direct athletic training coverage as primary athletic trainer for Football and Golf. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Leadership and Staff Management Oversee the Athletic Training and Sports Performance staff, including hiring, onboarding, training and day-to-day supervision. Conduct annual goal setting and performance reviews with each staff member, with regular check-ins throughout the year. Build and publish daily Athletic Training Clinic schedules and sport coverage assignments that balance student-athlete access to care with sustainable staff workloads. Oversee strength and conditioning and weight room operations in coordination with the sports performance staff. Serve on the Athletics Department Senior Leadership Team, contributing to departmental strategy, policy and decision-making. Campus and External Partnerships Serve as the athletics liaison to the campus Health Center and Accommodation Services, coordinating care, referrals, academic and physical accommodations, and return-to-learn plans for student-athletes. Serve as the primary liaison to the Team Physician, coordinating game coverage, on-campus clinics, referrals and standing orders. Serve as the primary liaison to the department's Physical Therapy partnership, coordinating in-house rehabilitation services and return-to-play communication. Clinical Care and Sport Coverage Serve as Head Athletic Trainer for Football and primary athletic trainer for Golf, including practice, competition and travel coverage. Provide prevention, evaluation, treatment, rehabilitation and return-to-play care consistent with the BOC Standards of Professional Practice and Massachusetts licensure requirements. Policy, Compliance and Administration Develop, maintain and annually review sports medicine policies and procedures, including emergency action plans, concussion management, catastrophic injury, heat illness and medication management protocols. Ensure compliance with NCAA, Northeast-10 and institutional health and safety legislation, including pre-participation exams, medical documentation and sickle cell trait screening. Oversee electronic medical records, injury tracking and secondary insurance claims processes. Manage the sports medicine and sports performance budgets, inventory, supplies and equipment. Promote student-athlete mental health resources and coordinate referrals with campus and external providers. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Required Qualifications Master's degree Board of Certification (BOC) Certified Athletic Trainer (ATC) Massachusetts Athletic Trainer license, or eligibility to be licensed in Massachusetts by the start date 3-5 years of experience as a certified athletic trainer, including football coverage At least 2 years of supervisory experience Current CPR/AED certification for the Professional Rescuer (or equivalent) Strong communication, organizational and conflict-resolution skills, and the ability to work with a diverse population of students, coaches and staff Valid driver's license and successful completion of a background check Preferred Qualifications 5-7 years of experience as a certified athletic trainer 3-5 years of supervisory experience NSCA Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS), or experience overseeing weight room operations Experience at the NCAA level Experience with electronic medical record systems and budget management Working Conditions and Physical Demands Irregular hours, including evenings, weekends and holidays, based on practice and competition schedules; flexible hours during summer months. Regular team travel, including overnight trips. Outdoor work in varied weather conditions. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds, stand for long periods, and respond quickly to emergencies on the field or court. AIC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply Now Related Searches: Athletics - Athletic Administration Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , 